<title>UK: Russia takes quarter of Cuba Jan/Feb sugar exports.</title>
<headline>Russia takes quarter of Cuba Jan/Feb sugar exports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cuba exported 1.07 million tonnes of raw sugar in the first two months of 1997, down on the 1.15 million exported in the same period in 1996, International Sugar Organization (ISO) data showed.</p>
<p>Russia took the lion's share of the exports in the period with 280,822 tonnes, or 26 percent of the total, of which 60,850 tonnes were taken in January and 219,972 in February.</p>
<p>Last January Russia imported 134,087 tonnes of Cuban raws and a further 428,180 tonnes in February.</p>
<p>China was in second place with a total 140,563 tonnes imported over January/February 1997, followed by Iran with 129,552 tonnes. Japan and Egypt also featured as significant importers of Cuban sugar.</p>
<p>Cuban sugar exports amounted to 277,310 tonnes in January 1996 and 877,547 tonnes in February 1996, ISO data showed. --Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
